#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Setup {#setup}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Import the tools used in both examples. Aer supports the intermediate "
"measurements introduced by gate cutting.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Small-scale simulator example {#small-scale-simulator-example}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use a six-qubit ring with two layers of entangling gates. The simulated "
"device has linear connectivity, so the ring's closing edge requires routing "
"unless it is cut.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-"
"inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following function creates RX rotation layers interleaved with CX gates "
"on alternating edges of the ring. Two repetitions give two boundary gates to"
" cut. Set the first two rotation layers to zero and the final layer to "
"$\\pi$. The ideal output is then $|1\\rangle^{\\otimes n}$, up to a global "
"phase.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Measure the average single-qubit Z expectation and the average adjacent ZZ "
"expectation, **including the periodic pair**:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"M_Z = \\frac{1}{n}\\sum_{i=0}^{n-1}\\langle Z_i\\rangle, \\qquad\n"
"C_{ZZ} = \\frac{1}{n}\\sum_{i=0}^{n-1}\\langle Z_i Z_{(i+1)\\bmod n}\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Their ideal values are $-1$ and $+1$, respectively. These parameters provide"
" a benchmark for the workflow; they do not demonstrate a classically "
"difficult computation.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Six-qubit periodic circuit with two boundary CX "
"gates](/docs/images/tutorials/periodic-boundary-conditions-with-circuit-"
"cutting/extracted-outputs/periodic-06-1.avif)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-"
"problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Create a device model with a linear coupling map. It supplies the "
"compilation target; the execution in Step 3 will be noiseless.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Add a **virtual connection** between the physical qubits at the ends of the "
"chain. Transpile once using this augmented coupling map and a CX basis. The "
"virtual connection prevents the transpiler from routing the boundary gates, "
"but the resulting circuit cannot run on the real device yet.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Find and cut the two boundary CX gates, apply the virtual layout to the "
"observables, and generate all decomposition terms with `num_samples=np.inf`."
" This makes the decomposition coefficients exact; the measurements still use"
" a finite number of shots.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, translate the experiments into the device's native gates and "
"correct their direction where needed. These passes preserve the physical "
"qubit layout and avoid repeating layout selection and routing for every "
"experiment. The helper returns the mapped observables needed for "
"reconstruction.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each CX decomposition has six terms. With two cuts and one shared Z "
"measurement basis, this produces $6^2=36$ experiments. The sampling overhead"
" is a different quantity: the squared sum of the absolute decomposition "
"coefficients is $9^2=81$. It describes the sampling cost of maintaining "
"precision under quasiprobability reconstruction. See the [sampling overhead "
"explanation](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-"
"cutting/explanation/index.html).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For comparison, transpile a measured copy of the uncut circuit using the "
"actual coupling map. `measure_all()` records the original logical qubits in "
"the `meas` register; transpilation preserves that classical-bit mapping, so "
"its counts can be evaluated with the original observables.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-"
"primitives}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Run both versions with the Aer Sampler V2 primitive. Each cut experiment "
"receives 10,000 shots, as does the single uncut circuit. The cut workflow "
"therefore uses 36 times as many shots in this comparison. Matching shots per"
" circuit does not match the total execution budget.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format "
"{#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Reconstruct each Pauli expectation value using the same mapped observables "
"and experiment order used during generation. Then average the first $n$ "
"values for $M_Z$ and the remaining $n$ values for $C_{ZZ}$. For the uncut "
"circuit, calculate the expectation values directly from the measured "
"counts.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Ideal, cut, and uncut expectation values from noiseless "
"simulation](/docs/images/tutorials/periodic-boundary-conditions-with-"
"circuit-cutting/extracted-outputs/periodic-16-1.avif)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The noiseless results should be close to the ideal values. Finite-shot "
"reconstruction can fluctuate, and a reconstructed estimate can lie outside "
"$[-1,1]$. Cutting does not improve an already noiseless result; this example"
" verifies the decomposition, layout mapping, and reconstruction before "
"execution on hardware.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Large-scale hardware example {#large-scale-hardware-example}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Reuse the workflow on the least-busy operational QPU with at least 120 "
"qubits. Select a longest shortest path in its undirected coupling graph: "
"each consecutive pair is connected, while the endpoints are far apart. This "
"adapts the chain to the selected device instead of relying on a fixed Eagle "
"layout. The code checks that the chain contains at least 30 qubits and that "
"its endpoints are not neighbors.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following block combines the four steps. Gate twirling, measurement "
"twirling, and dynamical decoupling are disabled for both versions. Both jobs"
" run in the same batch and receive the tutorial tag `TUT_CCPBC`. The cut "
"experiments still use more total shots, so compare both accuracy and QPU "
"usage.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Ideal, cut, and uncut expectation values measured on "
"ibm_boston](/docs/images/tutorials/periodic-boundary-conditions-with-"
"circuit-cutting/extracted-outputs/periodic-19-1.avif)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the recorded run on `ibm_boston`, the cut estimates were approximately "
"$M_Z=-0.923$ and $C_{ZZ}=0.896$, compared with $-0.611$ and $0.516$ for the "
"uncut circuit. Both cut estimates were closer to the ideal values of $-1$ "
"and $+1$.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Compare each result with its ideal value and inspect the circuit depths and "
"total QPU usage. Cutting removes the need to route the periodic gates, but "
"introduces intermediate operations and additional statistical uncertainty. "
"Hardware noise and calibration affect the comparison; an improvement is not "
"guaranteed. Repeated runs are needed to assess whether an observed "
"difference is statistically significant.\n"
msgstr ""

